  {
    "episode_id": 81189,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81189.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Good morning everybody and welcome to another edition of Community Matters here on 103-7-W-E-E-E-I. I'm your host, Scott Kordishi. Glad you could join us. Community Matters is the show that comes your way each and every Saturday morning and keeps you up to date and in touch with many of the great things happening in and around our communities here in the state of Rhode Island, also in eastern Connecticut and in southeastern Massachusetts. And this morning it gives us great pleasure to welcome to the program the Congressman for the First District of Rhode Island. Congressman Gabe Amo is with us. Congressman Amo, good morning. How are you? I'm great Scott. It's great to be on with you. Thanks for the invitation. Well, thanks so much for joining us, Congressman Ammo. I appreciate it. You are a native of Patucket Road Island, and it's always great to have a local guy on the show. Well, Congressman Ammo, so much is going on. I know in your neck of the woods down in Washington, D.C., and certainly affecting all of us throughout the nation, including here in Rhode Island. I guess You know, first things first, are there anything or things that you want to talk about on the show this morning that you feel are of the utmost",
