    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81189.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Look, I think first and foremost, what should be important to constituents across the first district to Rhode Island is just what's happening in Washington right now with regard to the new administration in the White House led by President Trump and how it's affecting us. At the end of the day, my number one priority is ensuring that the people of the first congressional district have a congressperson who is fighting for them, making sure that I prioritize the needs of everybody in Rhode Island as we do this work. And certainly over the last 70-plus days, there's been a lot of chaos, there's been a lot of confusion, a lot of consternation, and a real set of challenges to the people across America, but especially at home. That's mass firings of federal employees, uncertainty of funding for our key programs, research funding for our universities. And as we talk right now, we're on the precipice of an announcement from the president that is going to raise costs. and the cost of living for people across the district. So that's a table setter. It's a lot. It has been a lot over the last several days, but I will turn to you to",
