    "turn_text": "If not all want to root out ways for an abuse. But the challenge here is when you are making arbitrary decisions that really cut away at the effectiveness of any function, for example, if you say to the Department of Education, we are going to eliminate ourselves. What do you do? You will eliminate a function. When you say to the Social Security Administration, we are going to cut the number of staff who are answering the phones or the number of offices we have and add new requirements that make it difficult for people to achieve a benefit, you undermine the performance of a program. So my goal is to highlight to communicate out of those challenges, the real-life stories, to legislate, even if we can't pass the bills, it is incredibly important to raise the alarm wherever necessary and see who stands on which side. To work with our great State Attorney General and Peter Narona, and all of the litigation that they are leading on with Attorney General around the country. And we have to continue to find avenues to collaborate. And that's how I work across the aisle with",
